# Original magic items for the new classes and the optional systems.
# Format: (name, category, rarity, attunement, text)
A = "Requires Attunement"
ITEMS = [
# ================= CAPTAIN =================
("Signal Whistle of the Line", "Wondrous Item", "Common", None,
 "When you blow this brass whistle, every ally within 300 feet who knows your signals hears it clearly over any noise and understands one simple order, such as advance, hold, or fall back."),
("Marshal's Baton", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", A + " by a Captain",
 "While you hold this baton, the range of your Orders increases by 30 feet. Once per Short Rest, you can give an Order without spending a Command Die."),
("Standard of the Unbroken Company", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A + " by a Captain",
 "As a Bonus Action, you can plant this banner in the ground within 5 feet of you. While it stands, you and each ally within 30 feet of it have Advantage on saving throws against the Frightened condition, and when you give an Order to an ally within that area, the ally also gains Temporary Hit Points equal to your Intelligence modifier. The banner stays planted until a creature takes an action to pull it up. Once used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."),
("Field Map of the Hundred Battles", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", A + " by a Captain",
 "When you share a Battle Plan, you can study this map for 1 minute. Each creature that receives the plan also gains a +2 bonus to its AC during the first round of the next combat that it fights before its next Long Rest."),
("Gorget of Command", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", A + " by a Captain",
 "While you wear this steel gorget, your Command Dice are one size larger (a d12 stays a d12), and you regain one expended Command Die when you roll Initiative."),
("Spyglass of the Watch Captain", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", None,
 "Objects seen through this spyglass are magnified to ten times their size. As a Magic action, you can study a creature you see through it for 1 minute and learn its AC, its Speed, and whether it has any Resistances, Vulnerabilities, or Immunities."),
# ================= APOTHECARY =================
("Ever-Clean Mortar", "Wondrous Item", "Common", None,
 "Anything ground in this stone mortar never spoils and never mixes with what was ground in it before. It cleans itself between uses."),
("Bandolier of Quick Vials", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", None,
 "This leather bandolier holds up to ten vials, which never break while they are in it. While you wear it, drawing a vial or a potion from it is part of the action or Bonus Action you use to drink, feed, or throw it."),
("Alembic of Lasting Brews", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A + " by an Apothecary",
 "When you prepare concoctions with this silver alembic, choose one of them. That concoction doesn't lose its power when you finish your next Long Rest; it lasts until you finish your third Long Rest. You can have only one lasting concoction at a time."),
("Gloves of the Steady Pour", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", A + " by an Apothecary",
 "While you wear these gloves, you can throw a bomb or make a Vial Toss at a point or a creature up to 60 feet away, and you add your Proficiency Bonus to the damage of your Vial Toss."),
("Reagent Satchel of the Wandering Healer", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", A + " by an Apothecary",
 "This satchel always holds the herbs and salts you need. When you finish a Long Rest, you prepare one more concoction than normal. Once per Long Rest, when you use Field Brewing, you can prepare two concoctions instead of one."),
("Mask of the Plague Doctor", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A,
 "While you wear this beaked mask, you have Immunity to the Poisoned condition, you have Resistance to Poison damage, and you can't contract diseases. You also have Advantage on Wisdom (Medicine) checks."),
# ================= SHAPER =================
("Element Stone", "Wondrous Item", "Common", None,
 "This smooth stone is warm, cold, crackling, or heavy, depending on the element of the last Shaper who held it. While you hold it, you can use Minor Shaping without speaking, and its effects are a little brighter, colder, louder, or stronger, as the GM decides."),
("Bracers of the Focused Will", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", A + " by a Shaper",
 "While you wear these bracers, you gain a +1 bonus to attack rolls with your Elemental Bolt, and the range of your Elemental Bolt increases to 150 feet."),
("Strain Ward Amulet", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A + " by a Shaper",
 "This amulet has 3 charges and regains all of them at dawn. When you use a Surge, you can expend 1 charge to gain 1 less Strain from it (minimum 0)."),
("Crown of the Four Answers", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", A + " by a Shaper",
 "While you wear this crown, you can change the element of your Attunement when you finish a Short Rest, instead of when you gain a Shaper level. Your shaping save DC also increases by 1."),
("Cinder Heart", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A + " by a Shaper",
 "This red crystal beats like a heart. Once on each of your turns when you deal element damage with a Surge, you can add your Wisdom modifier to the damage against one creature. If you Overstrain while you carry it, the crystal goes dark until the next dawn and the benefit ends until then."),
("Mantle of the Calm Storm", "Wondrous Item", "Legendary", A + " by a Shaper",
 "While you wear this gray mantle, your Strain Limit increases by 2. Once per Long Rest, you can Overstrain without gaining a level of Exhaustion."),
# ================= SPIRITBINDER =================
("Spirit Bell", "Wondrous Item", "Common", None,
 "When you ring this small bell, you can tell whether a spirit, a ghost, or a bound spirit is within 30 feet of you. The bell rings by itself when such a creature comes within 10 feet of it."),
("Collar of the Bound", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", A + " by a Spiritbinder",
 "You can place this spectral collar on your bound spirit. While it wears the collar, the spirit gains a +1 bonus to its AC and to its attack rolls."),
("Lantern of Returning", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A + " by a Spiritbinder",
 "When your bound spirit drops to 0 Hit Points while you carry this lantern, it returns to the lantern instead of to your soul. You can call it back from the lantern as a Bonus Action, without expending a Hit Point Die. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn."),
("Talisman of the Shared Breath", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A + " by a Spiritbinder",
 "While you wear this talisman, you regain one expended Bond Point when your bound spirit reduces a creature to 0 Hit Points. You can regain a Bond Point this way only once per turn."),
("Ring of the Twin Soul", "Ring", "Very Rare", A + " by a Spiritbinder",
 "While you wear this ring, your bound spirit's Hit Point maximum increases by twice your Spiritbinder level, and you can see through its eyes and hear what it hears as a Bonus Action, until the start of your next turn."),
("Reliquary of the First Binder", "Wondrous Item", "Legendary", A + " by a Spiritbinder",
 "This bone box holds the ashes of the first Spiritbinder. While you carry it, you gain two extra Bond Points, and your bound spirit can take the Attack action on its turn without a command from you."),
# ================= MARKS (optional rules) =================
("Charm of the Slow Tide", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A,
 "This braided charm holds back a Mark. When the track of one of your Marks would grow, you can let the charm take the growth instead. The track doesn't grow, and the charm cracks; it mends after 7 days. The charm can't stop a track from reaching 5, and it doesn't work on a Mark that you have given in to."),
("Mirror of Hidden Burdens", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", None,
 "When a creature looks into this hand mirror, it sees the shapes of any Marks that it carries, including hidden ones, but not their names or their tracks. The GM describes each shape in a few words."),
("Censer of Confession", "Wondrous Item", "Very Rare", None,
 "When a creature spends 8 hours in prayer or quiet thought beside this burning censer and honestly confesses what feeds one of its Marks, the track of that Mark drops by 1. A creature can benefit from the censer only once in 30 days."),
# ================= BONDS (optional rules) =================
("Twin Lockets", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", None,
 "These two silver lockets are made as a pair. While two bonded partners each wear one of them, they can use their Bond on each other at any distance on the same plane, as long as each knows that the other is in danger."),
("Knot of the Unbroken Bond", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", None,
 "When a strain would make your bond die one size smaller, you can untie this cord instead. The bond die doesn't shrink. The knot crumbles to dust."),
("Oathstone", "Wondrous Item", "Rare", A,
 "Two creatures who both touch this stone while they swear an Oath Bond can attune to it together, and it counts as one attunement for both. While both partners carry the stone and the bond die of their Oath Bond is a d10, the die can't become smaller from strain. A broken oath still makes it smaller."),
# ================= TECHNIQUES (optional rules) =================
("Training Weights of the Old Master", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", A,
 "While you wear these iron bracelets, you gain one extra technique point. You regain it as you regain your other technique points. A creature gains the benefit of only one pair of these bracelets at a time."),
("Stance Sash", "Wondrous Item", "Uncommon", None,
 "While you wear this silk sash, entering a Stance technique doesn't cost you a technique point once per Short Rest."),
("Scroll of Hidden Forms", "Scroll", "Rare", None,
 "This scroll holds the secrets of a fighting school. When you study it for 8 hours, you learn one technique of your choice that you qualify for. The scroll then turns to dust."),
]
